# Financial Control — Frontend Rules

Operational instructions for Cursor. Do not create new architectural decisions here.

Authority: `AGENTS.md` → `docs/20–28` → `docs/CODING_STANDARDS.md` → this file.

Official stack: Angular 22.x, TypeScript strict, standalone components. Do not invent tutorial versions.

---

## 1. Responsibility

The Angular app talks to the backend only through `/api/v1`.

It must not:

- access PostgreSQL;
- implement authoritative financial rules;
- depend on Java/JPA/Spring types;
- use the browser timezone to decide financial rules.

---

## 2. Feature organization

Organize by the real domain:

```text
features/accounts
features/expenses
features/incomes
features/transfers
features/payments
features/credit-cards
features/financial-goals
```

Do not create a generic `transactions` feature.

Do not automatically create four folders per feature.

If a feature only needs:

```text
expenses-page.ts
expenses-page.html
expenses.service.ts
```

keep it that way. Add `components/`, `pages/`, `services/`, `models/` only when there are enough files to justify them.

Shared code must be genuinely reusable. `core/` is for app-wide infrastructure (auth, HTTP), not a dumping ground.

---

## 3. Components and services

Components present UI and call feature services.

Services own HTTP. Components do not call `HttpClient` directly.

Do not create `AppService`, `DataService`, `HelperService`, `GenericCrudService`, or `BaseComponent`.

Do not create `ExpenseStateService` to pass one value between parent and child.

HTTP URLs belong in services and environment config, never hard-coded `localhost:8080` in feature code.

Models represent the JSON API (`ExpenseResponse`), not Java entities.

---

## 4. State, signals, RxJS

Local component state first.

Signals when they make local UI state clearer. Not every variable needs to be a signal.

RxJS where Angular already exposes observables. Do not convert every observable into a signal automatically.

No NgRx in V1.

No global state by default.

---

## 5. Forms, money, errors

Typed reactive forms for complex forms.

Frontend validation is UX only.

Format money for display (`R$ 1.234,50`) without changing the numeric value.

Map API errors from the official `docs/25-api.md` format (`status`, `code`, `message`, `fields`). Do not invent a second error shape.

Pagination fields from the API: `items`, `totalItems`, `totalPages`. Do not expect Spring `content` / `totalElements`.

---

## 6. Routing

Feature routes: `expenses.routes.ts`.

`GET`-style screens: `/accounts`, `/expenses`, `/credit-cards`.

Guards for auth/access only. Guards are not security and not business rules.

Lazy-load meaningful features, not tiny screens.

---

## 7. UI and CSS

Use Angular Material directly. Do not wrap every button/input/table on day one.

Component-scoped styles. No `!important` as default.

Accessibility is required: semantic HTML, labels, keyboard, focus.

---

## 8. Before creating a component or service

1. Is there a real UI/application responsibility?
2. Is it reused for a real reason, not because two templates look similar once?
3. Can this stay in the existing page/service?

Do not add npm packages because they are popular.

Details: `docs/CODING_STANDARDS.md`, `docs/21-arquitetura-do-sistema.md`.
